      "unitRules": [
        {
          "name": "Translocation Portal",
          "text": "A model equipped with a Translocation Portal can be assigned the following Combat Assignment: Invasion Mission. -- Once assigned an Invasion Mission in the Reserves Sub-Phase, a model must be immediately placed onto the Battlefield by the Controlling player. The Model may be placed anywhere along the Battlefield Edge that is within the Controlling Player's Deployment Zone. This deployment can trigger the Intercept Advanced Reaction, but any attacks made at the Model are made as Snap Shots. -- In the Movement Phase, a model with an Invasion Mission can be selected and must then move up to a number of inches equal to its Movement Characteristic straight forwards without turning. At this point a Combat Air Patrol can be declared by the Reactive Player. Once any Combat Air Patrol Reactions have been resolved, the Controlling Player may select a Unit entirely composed of models with the Infantry Type in reserves that has no more than 15 models (counting models with the Bulky (X) special rule as a number of models equal to the value of X attached to that special rule) that is in reserves or on the battlefield wholly within 12\" of the Model with the Invasion Mission and apply the following depending on that unit's location: --- In Reserves: Place the unit anywhere on the battlefield wholly within 12\" of the base of the Model with the Invasion Mission. A unit placed on the battlefield this way cannot triger Reactions and cannot move further in the current Movement Phase but is counted as having moved for the purpose of any rules and special rules. --- On the Battlefield: Remove the unit from the Battlefield and place it in Reserves. -- In the Shooting Phase, a model that has been assigned an Invasion Mission may make Shooting Attacks, but must make all attacks as Snap Shots. At the end of the Controlling Player's Shooting Phase, the Model assigned an Invasion Mission is removed from play and returned to Aerial Reserves."
        }
      ],
